# Trivy Ignore File
# This file contains CVEs that are intentionally ignored during security scans

# CVE-2026-102828: simple-git: critical vulnerability (Trivy CRITICAL)
# CVE-2026-102829: @simple-git/argv-parser: critical vulnerability (Trivy CRITICAL)
# Severity: CRITICAL
# Affected: simple-git 3.36.0 / @simple-git/argv-parser 1.1.1
#   (usr/local/lib/node_modules/difit/node_modules/)
# Fixed in: simple-git 4.0.1 / @simple-git/argv-parser 2.0.1
# Reason: difit declares simple-git ^3.28.0 and has no release supporting simple-git 4.x,
#   so updating npm/global.json cannot pull the fix. An npm override would force a major
#   bump into difit untested. Temporarily accept while waiting for difit to support 4.x.
# Risk: difit is a local diff viewer run by the developer against their own repositories;
#   untrusted git arguments are not passed to it in this image. This exception does not fix it.
# Expected resolution: Remove these entries once difit depends on simple-git >= 4.0.1.
# Tracking: https://github.com/keito4/config/issues/1339
# Note 2026-10-10: Accepted per owner decision in monthly maintenance (C).
# Note 2026-11-11: Re-verified in monthly maintenance. difit is still 5.0.12 with
#   simple-git ^3.28.0 (checked against the npm registry), and a scan with this entry
#   removed still reported both CVEs as the only CRITICAL findings, so the exception
#   is still required. Extended to the next monthly maintenance window.
# Review date: 2026-12-10
CVE-2026-102828
CVE-2026-102829

